sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Op as Postman / operator
  participant PF as kubectl port-forward<br/>127.0.0.1:18085
  participant OIDC as local-oidc fixture<br/>(ClusterIP only)
  participant GW as Traefik Gateway<br/>192.168.49.2:30000
  participant API as control-api
  participant JWKS as JWKS endpoint

  Note over OIDC: No HTTPRoute reaches this service.<br/>An identity provider that anyone can<br/>call from outside the cluster is not one.

  Op->>PF: start forward to svc/local-oidc
  PF->>OIDC: tunnel established
  Op->>PF: GET /token?roles=tenant_developer&projects=<project>
  PF->>OIDC: forwarded
  OIDC->>OIDC: sign RS256, 15 minute expiry<br/>iss = in-cluster service URL
  OIDC-->>Op: { access_token }

  Note over Op: The issuer claim is the in-cluster URL,<br/>not 127.0.0.1. That is why a token from the<br/>Phase 4 Compose fixture on port 18080<br/>is rejected here with a bare 401.

  Op->>GW: request + Host: control-plane.test<br/>+ Authorization: Bearer <token>
  GW->>API: routed by HTTPRoute
  API->>JWKS: fetch signing keys (cached)
  JWKS-->>API: public key set
  API->>API: verify signature, issuer, audience
  API->>API: check role and project membership

  alt Role and membership satisfied
    API-->>Op: 200 / 202
  else Signature valid, membership absent
    API-->>Op: 403 PROJECT_ACCESS_DENIED
  else No token
    API-->>Op: 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
  end
